<title>INDIA: India's Escotel wins approval for $129 mln ECB.</title>
<headline>India's Escotel wins approval for $129 mln ECB.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Finance Ministry has given its approval to Escotel Mobile Communications Ltd to raise $129 million through external commercial borrowing, the company said in a statement received on Saturday.</p>
<p>It said Chase Manhattan was arranging the $129 loan, while Infrastructure Leasing &amp; Financial Services Ltd was arranging a 1.25 billion rupee requirement.</p>
<p>Escotel is a joint venture between Escorts Limited and First Pacific Company Ltd of Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Escotel plans to extend its cellullar service from 23 cities to a further 10 towns and three cities this year, and raise its customer base to 60,000. ($1.00 = 35.8 rupees)</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom (91) 22 265 9000</p>
